60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Candidate A is a beautiful vision, but it requires the very technicians we have lost. Candidate D, however, aligns with our strong glasshouse crew.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Sakura,,Candidate D uses the greenhouse! And I found out the agency pays for that! That means they can spend their money on other things!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Candidate A is like a catalogue... the closeout files showed that those kinds of projects actually deliver their results and stay useful.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Candidate B is out. Spectroscopy? I just saw the logs. That suite is a disaster. It'll be a total waste of time.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,Candidate D is impossible. I found that the glasshouse blocks are booked solid for two more cycles. They cannot start their trials.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, that is a vital observation. We must not lead a researcher into a wall. Let us reconsider the others.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Sakura,,Oh no! No greenhouse for D? That's a bummer! What about Candidate C? Do they need a lot of shipping?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,Candidate C... they use live animals. The portfolio review said those projects overran their schedules twice as often. I'm scared to pick them.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,@Daisuke is right for once. C is a risk. A is just data and sequences. It doesn't need the broken equipment or the full greenhouse.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,Candidate A relies on the national repository and computing. My findings show the computing agreement is stable and the repository is functioning.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"Candidate A requires the ""trained hands"" of the field, but the data processing is where the current strength lies. It is a sustainable path.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"If A just needs computers and some soil, that's way cheaper than shipping things across the world! I like A!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think A is the safest. It's the kind of project that actually finishes. I'll vote for A.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"It's the only one that doesn't hit a known bottleneck. No spectroscopy, no animal colony delays, no greenhouse queues. A is the only logical choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,I agree. Candidate A's requirements align with the current available capacity of the national infrastructure. It is the most viable option.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,It is a rare joy when we find a path that serves both the science and the people. I am in agreement.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! We all agree! This was like a puzzle and we solved it!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm glad... I'm glad we're all on the same page.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,Finally. Let's just vote and finish this.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,The evidence is conclusive. Let us proceed to the vote.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
